<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Yves Montand</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1963</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording (released as a single in 1964)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Milva</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1965</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Quilapayún, Basta</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1969</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Grup Yorum, Haziranda Ölmek Zor / Berivan</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1988</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Turkish translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hannes Wader singt Arbeiterlieder</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1977</span><span class="sg-chain-h">German version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Zupfgeigenhansel, Miteinander</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1982</span><span class="sg-chain-h">free adaptation with a reluctant, war-weary partisan</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ciwan Haco, Çaw Bella</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1989</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Kurmanji Kurdish version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Goran Bregović, Champagne for Gypsies</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2012</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Money Heist, television series</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2017</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used in, sung many times by the characters</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Songs of Resistance 1942–2018 (Marc Ribot with Tom Waits)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2018</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Rebella Ciao (Extinction Rebellion)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2019</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new words on the same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Pilla Chao, in the film Businessman</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2012</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Rice-weeders' song of the mondine</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">late 19th century (earliest written version 1906)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted from, with different words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Koilen (Dus Zekele Koilen), recorded by Mishka Ziganoff</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1919</span><span class="sg-chain-h">possible source of the melody</span></li></ul></section>
